## 2. The Metal Arch Trellis (Most Decorative)

If you want something that looks stunning AND produces fruit, a metal arch trellis is your answer. Blackberries trained over a wrought-iron garden arch create a beautiful entry point to a flower garden or veggie patch.

[![Decorative metal arch trellis covered in ripe blackberries and raspberries framing a colorful garden pathway]({{ site.baseurl }}/assets/images/home-decor/metal-arch-trellis-blackberries.jpg)](https://pin.it/55Wf2YjlO)

### Best Metal Arch Trellises to Buy (USA)

| Product | Price | Where to Buy |
|---|---|---|
| Amagabeli Garden Arch (7 ft) | ~$45 | Amazon |
| Gardman Rust-Resistant Arch | ~$60 | Walmart / Wayfair |
| Panacea Products Metal Arch | ~$55 | Home Depot |

### How to Train Berries Over an Arch

1. **Plant one blackberry or thornless blackberry cane** on each side of the arch base.
2. **In year one**, let the canes grow upright. Loosely tie them to the arch sides.
3. **In year two**, begin bending the longest canes over the top of the arch. Secure with plant clips or zip ties.
4. **Prune spent canes** after fruiting to keep new growth coming.

Recommended variety: **'Triple Crown' thornless blackberry** — easy to train, heavy fruiter, widely available at Burpee.com or your local garden center.

