## 3. The Raised Bed Fence Trellis (Best for Urban Gardens)

No open yard? No problem. This setup uses a raised wooden planter box built against an existing fence or wall. Berry canes grow upward using stakes or wire, and the fence acts as a natural support.

[![Raised wooden planter bed with raspberries and blackberries trained up a backyard fence using bamboo stakes]({{ site.baseurl }}/assets/images/home-decor/raised-bed-fence-trellis-berries.jpg)](https://pin.it/55Wf2YjlO)

### Materials List

| Item | Cost | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Cedar raised bed kit (4x1 ft) | $30–$50 | Amazon or Home Depot |
| Bamboo stakes (4 ft, 10-pack) | $8–$12 | Walmart / Amazon |
| 20-gauge galvanized wire | $10 | Home Depot |
| Eye hooks (pack of 20) | $5 | Hardware store |

### Build Steps

1. **Assemble or build your raised bed** along the fence line (at least 12 inches deep for berries).
2. **Screw eye hooks into the fence** at 12-inch intervals, at heights of 1 ft, 2 ft, and 3 ft.
3. **Thread galvanized wire** through the eye hooks to create three horizontal support lines.
4. **Fill the bed** with a mix of topsoil and compost (50/50).
5. **Plant canes 18 inches apart** and tie them to the wire as they grow.

This method works perfectly in a 6×1 ft space and can support 6–8 cane plants easily.

